 ## License
 
 This project is licensed under the [Apache License 2.0](../LICENSE).
+
+### Optional durable failure isolation
+
+`agent.failure_isolation_enabled` defaults to `false`. Enabling it requires an
+explicit non-secret `agent.failure_isolation_context` naming the exact approved
+workflow/source context. It currently requires the native Linear adapter's issue
+comment read/create operations. Unsupported capabilities and context changes
+hold dispatch; they do not silently fall back to volatile retries.
+
+The orchestrator is the sole native state writer. It appends compact
+`symphony-failure-v1:` JSON events to the existing authoritative issue, with issue
+ID, context, sequence, unique revision, parent revision and failure streak. It
+reads all comment pages and verifies the event chain before dispatch, writes an
+in-flight event before any worker/setup starts, and verifies each append by exact
+readback. An unknown write is never blindly repeated. Forks, gaps, malformed
+records and orphaned in-flight events after restart hold dispatch. Normal turns,
+heartbeats and token activity do not reset failure counts. Three consecutive
+confirmed identical typed failures block; typed permission denial and operator
+input block immediately. Opaque failures hold without inventing a confirmed
+count. Raw hook output, exception messages and authentication settings are not
+written to these events or exposed through the public Issue prompt object.
+
+Issue comment writers are trusted operators, not an authenticated state store.
+Preserve these events: deleting every event is indistinguishable from a new issue;
+editing/forging an event may hold the chain. This implementation does not claim
+protection against privileged record deletion or competing native parents.
+After resolving and fencing the prior attempt, an operator can use
+`FailureIsolation.resume/2` on the exact current event with a new non-secret
+progress reference, then append its `FailureIsolation.body/1` through the existing
+Linear comment tool and verify readback. Never treat an ordinary reopen or source
+context change as automatic progress; retained holds require reconciliation.
+The helper is not a new scheduler, daemon or local ledger. Packaging and effective
+activation of the changed native modules require the separate owner's exact
+source/artifact binding; the old runtime asset alone does not include this change.
